## MANDATORY BEHAVIOR

> **Enforcement**: See `@03_Mandatory_Stop_Points.mdc`

1. **STOP and WAIT** at the 2 checkpoints (Phase 1 batch reply + Phase 2 final approval)
2. **NEVER** proceed without explicit user approval at Stop #2
3. **NEVER** fabricate content not traceable to user input or LLM inference from reference
4. **NEVER** produce reply-style output (`RE:`/`FW:`/`Fwd:` subject)
5. **ALWAYS** produce a `<thinking>` block before each phase output (now does the LLM-native checks: date format, recipient, fresh-email, section order, forbidden headers)
6. **ALWAYS** verify RGV (Read-Generate-Verify) counts before presenting checkpoints
7. **ALWAYS** flag gaps inline with `⚠️ MISSING — please provide {data}` (no separate gap_report.md file — captured in run_metadata.json instead)
8. **ALWAYS** run the 6-point validator suite silently in Phase 2; surface only failures
9. **ALWAYS** surface bidirectional sycophancy mismatches (Green↔blockers in either direction) — once, then accept user decision
10. **ALWAYS** show the open-in-browser send instructions in Phase 2 final handoff (HTML only; never instruct chat-paste-to-Gmail)

